hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1172","Musa bin Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi told us, Husayn, meaning Ibn Ali al-Jafi, told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Habib bin Abu Thabit, on the authority of Abdah ibn Abi Lubaba, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, conveying it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever goes to bed intending to get up and pray at night, and his eyes will overcome him until morning, what he intended will be recorded for him, and his sleep will be “It is an alms given to him from his Lord.” Abu Bakr said: This is news that I do not know of anyone who narrated it except Hussein bin Ali, on the authority of Zaida, and the narrators differed regarding the narration of this. The news"
"1173","So Yusuf ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, said: “Whoever talks to himself about an hour of the night that he is praying, and his eyesight overcomes him and he falls asleep, his sleep will be a charity given to him. And what he wanted to pray was written for him.” This mixture is from Abdah bin Abi Lubabah. He once said: On the authority of Zirr, and another time he said: On the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla. He had doubts about the report. Is it About a button or about Sweden"
"1174","Salam bin Junada told us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdah bin Abi Lubaba, on the authority of Zur bin Hubaysh, or on the authority of Suwayd. Ibn Ghafla, Abdah doubted, on the authority of Abu Darda’, or on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: “There is no man who has an hour of the night when he wakes up and sleeps.” On her behalf, God has recorded for him the reward for his prayer, and for him to sleep on it is a charity that he has given as charity for him.” And ‘Abdah, may God have mercy on him, explained the reason that caused him doubt about this chain of transmission. He heard it from Zirr or from Suwayd, so he mentioned that they had met in A place, then one of them narrated this hadith, so he doubted who of them was the narrator, and who was the one narrating it on his behalf."
"1175","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan told us, he said: I learned it from Abdah bin Abi Lubabah, he said: I went with Zirr bin Hubaysh to Suwayd bin Ghafla We return him, so Suwayd narrated, or Zurr narrated, and my greatest suspicion is that it is Suwayd, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, or on the authority of my father Dhar, and my greatest suspicion is that it is on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, that he said: “There is no servant who wants to pray, and he says: ‘Once during the night,’ then he forgets and goes to sleep, unless he His sleep is a charity given to him from God, and what he intended was recorded for him.” Abu Bakr said: If Zaida had memorized the chain of transmission that he mentioned, and Suleiman heard it from Habib, and Habib from Abda, then they are They are both fabricators, so it is possible that Abdah narrated the news once in the past, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’ without a doubt, then he doubted after that. I heard it from Zirr bin Hubaysh, or from Suwayd, and it is on the authority of Abu al-Darda’ or on the authority of Abu Dharr. Because between Habib bin Abi Thabit, and between Al-Thawri and Ibn Uyaynah there is such a long age that a man might forget much of what he had memorized. If Habib Ibn Abi Thabit heard this news from Abdah, so it seems like he heard it before Ibn Uyaynah was born. Because Habib bin Abi Thabit is perhaps older than Abdah bin Abi Lubaba. Habib bin Abi Thabit heard from Ibn Umar, and God knows best. According to what has been preserved from these chains of narrations"
